<article class="env-lemma" id="07U8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07U8">Lemma <span data-tag="07U8">69.11.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be an affine morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. In this case $f_*\mathcal{F} \cong Rf_*\mathcal{F}$ is a quasi-coherent sheaf, and for every diagram (<a href="/tag/073J" data-tag="073J">69.11.0.1</a>) we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  g^*f_*\mathcal{F} = f'_*(g')^*\mathcal{F}.  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By the discussion surrounding (<a href="/tag/071Z" data-tag="071Z">69.3.0.1</a>) this reduces to the case of an affine morphism of schemes which is treated in Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/02KG" data-tag="02KG">30.5.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>